<title>QATAR: Qatar welcomes OPEC accord.</title>
<headline>Qatar welcomes OPEC accord.</headline>
<dateline>DOHA 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Qatar's Energy and Industry Minister Abdullah bin Hamad al-Attiyah welcomed OPEC's decision on Thursday to freeze output quotas for six months.</p>
<p>He said OPEC's decision to continue with a production ceiling set at 25.03 million barrels per day (bpd) would help stabilise world oil markets and prices.</p>
<p>&quot;This agreement is what we expected before the conference began and is what we supported,&quot; Attiyah told the official Qatari news agency after the meeting ended in Vienna.</p>
<p>OPEC member Qatar has a quota of 389,000 bpd though actual output has been running closer to 500,000 bpd.</p>
</text>
